              "segment": {
                "start_index": 270,
                "end_index": 699,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The Baseline Calculation (Simplified)\nTo establish a starting point, we can use standard physiological averages:\n* **Average lifespan:** 80 years (typical for developed countries)\n* **Average hours awake:** 16 hours per day (assuming 8 hours of sleep, as we do not blink while sleeping)\n* **Average adult blink rate:** **15 blinks per minute** (the typical resting rate for a healthy adult is between 15 and 20 blinks per minute)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 701,
                "end_index": 807,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Using these standard assumptions:\n* **Blinks per hour:** 15 blinks/min \u00d7 60 minutes = **900 blinks/hour**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 701,
                "end_index": 887,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Using these standard assumptions:\n* **Blinks per hour:** 15 blinks/min \u00d7 60 minutes = **900 blinks/hour**\n* **Blinks per day:** 900 blinks/hour \u00d7 16 awake hours = **14,400 blinks/day**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 701,
                "end_index": 975,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Using these standard assumptions:\n* **Blinks per hour:** 15 blinks/min \u00d7 60 minutes = **900 blinks/hour**\n* **Blinks per day:** 900 blinks/hour \u00d7 16 awake hours = **14,400 blinks/day**\n* **Blinks per year:** 14,400 blinks/day \u00d7 365.25 days = **~5.26 million blinks/year**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1079,
                "end_index": 1203,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*(If we use a slightly higher average of 17.5 blinks per minute, the lifetime total climbs to roughly **490 million blinks**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1409,
                "end_index": 1460,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Infant and Child Blinking Rates\nBabies barely blink"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1462,
                "end_index": 1627,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Newborns and infants only blink about **2 to 4 times per minute** because their eyes are smaller (less surface area to dry out) and they have a more stable tear film"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1629,
                "end_index": 1739,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This rate rises slowly throughout childhood, only reaching the full adult rate of 15+ around early adolescence"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
